# User-facing copy (in-game / tutorial)

When writing or editing **player-visible text** — tutorial dialogue (`tutorial_guide.json`, `gen_tutorial_guide.py`), Kanon bubble copy, toasts, overlays, i18n `tutorial.*` keys, card UI hints, etc.:

## Do

- Write as **in-world teaching**: explain what the player sees and what to do **now**.
- Match the tone of existing tutorial references in `i18n.js` (`intro_*`, `setup_*`, `t1_*`): clear, friendly, rule-focused.
- Use game terms consistently: **Main Phase**, **Live Phase**, **Performance**, **Success** pile, **Hearts**, **Energy**, **Stage**, **mulligan**.

## Do not

- Mention **prior versions**, redesigns, or “how it used to work”.
- Use **meta** framing: “real turn vs reading rules”, “for this lesson”, “advanced lessons later”, “we changed X”, “new feature”, “unlike before”.
- Break the fourth wall about the tutorial being a tutorial (except where the UI literally says Tutorial / Exit to Title).

## Examples

| Avoid | Prefer |
|-------|--------|
| “You'll play a real turn, not just read rules!” | “I'll teach you the basics as we play.” |
| “Pick **You go first** for this lesson.” | “Tap **Go first** to play first.” |
| “We'll cover skills in advanced lessons!” | “Skills and baton pass come up naturally as you play.” |

Apply the same rules when mirroring copy to `tutorial_ja.json` or localized `tutorial.*` strings.

## i18n (required for all player-visible text)

Supported locales live in `i18n.js` (`LOCALES`, **en** + **ja** + **es** + **ko** + **zh** + **th** + **pt** + **fr**). **Every new or changed player-facing string must ship in all locales in the same change** — not English-only.

### Korean (required — do not skip)

Korean (`STRINGS.ko` / `locales/ko.json` / `tutorial_ko.json`) is a **first-class locale**, same as Spanish and Japanese. **Every new or changed player-facing string must include Korean in the same change** — menus, missions, toasts, overlays, news posts, and JS-built UI. Do not ship English-only or en+ja+es without `ko`.

Source of truth for KO UI copy is `locales/ko.json` → inject via `python scripts/inject_i18n_ko.py` when using that workflow; otherwise keep `STRINGS.ko` in `i18n.js` in sync with `locales/ko.json`.

### Chinese / zh-Hans (required — do not skip)

Simplified Chinese (`zh`, `document.documentElement.lang = zh-Hans`) is a **first-class locale**. **Every new or changed player-facing string must include Chinese in the same change** — menus, missions, toasts, overlays, news posts, tutorials, logs, stamps, and JS-built UI. Do not ship en+ja+es+ko without `zh`.

| Surface | Chinese files / fields |
|---------|------------------------|
| UI strings | `locales/zh.json` → `python scripts/inject_i18n_zh.py` → `STRINGS.zh` |
| Names / songs | `locales/zh_names.json` / `locales/zh_songs.json` → `python scripts/inject_i18n_zh_maps.py` |
| Card rules text | `cards.json` → `text_zh` (brackets: `[入场时]`, `[Live开始]`, `[起动]`, `[永续]`, `[每回合1次]`, …) |
| Tutorial | `tutorial_zh.json` via `build_tutorial_locale_json.py --locale zh` |
| Logs / prompts | `log_i18n.js` ZH rules (`localizeLogMessageZh` / `localizePromptTextZh`) |
| News | `news.json` posts → `title.zh` / `body.zh` |
| Stamps | `stamps_i18n.json` → `zh` (builder / `inject_stamps_zh.py`) |

See `docs/locales/ZH_PROGRESS.md` and `docs/locales/ZH_NAMES.md`.

### Thai (required — do not skip)

Thai (`th`, `document.documentElement.lang = 'th'`) is a **first-class locale**, same enforcement as Korean and Chinese. **Every new or changed player-facing string must include Thai in the same change** — menus, missions, toasts, overlays, news posts, tutorials, logs, stamps, and JS-built UI. Do not ship en+ja+es+ko+zh without `th`.

Infrastructure (`LOCALE_ORDER`, `inject_i18n_th.py`, `inject_i18n_th_maps.py`, `validate_i18n.php`, flag asset) exists as of M0; the actual `locales/th.json` / `locales/th_names.json` / `locales/th_songs.json` content ships starting at M1 — see `docs/locales/TH_PROGRESS.md` for current milestone status before assuming a given surface already has Thai coverage.

| Surface | Thai files / fields |
|---------|----------------------|
| UI strings | `locales/th.json` → `python scripts/inject_i18n_th.py` → `STRINGS.th` |
| Names / songs | `locales/th_names.json` / `locales/th_songs.json` → `python scripts/inject_i18n_th_maps.py` |
| Card rules text | `cards.json` → `text_th` (brackets: `[เมื่อเข้าสนาม]`, `[เริ่ม Live]`, `[เปิดใช้]`, `[ต่อเนื่อง]`, `[เทิร์นละ 1 ครั้ง]`, `[เซ็นเตอร์]`, …) |
| Tutorial | `tutorial_th.json` via `build_tutorial_locale_json.py --locale th` |
| Logs / prompts | `log_i18n.js` TH rules (`localizeLogMessageTh` / `localizePromptTextTh`) |
| News | `news.json` posts → `title.th` / `body.th` |
| Stamps | `stamps_i18n.json` → `th` (builder / `inject_stamps_th.py`) |

See `docs/locales/TH_PROGRESS.md` and `docs/locales/TH_NAMES.md`.

### Brazilian Portuguese / pt-BR (required — do not skip)

Brazilian Portuguese (`pt`, `document.documentElement.lang = 'pt-BR'`) is a **first-class locale**, same enforcement as Korean, Chinese, and Thai. **Every new or changed player-facing string must include Portuguese in the same change** — menus, missions, toasts, overlays, news posts, logs, stamps, and JS-built UI. Do not ship en+ja+es+ko+zh+th without `pt`.

| Surface | Portuguese files / fields |
|---------|---------------------------|
| UI strings | `locales/pt.json` → `python scripts/inject_i18n_pt.py` → `STRINGS.pt` |
| Card rules text | `cards.json` → `text_pt` (brackets: `[Ao Entrar]`, `[Início de Live]`, `[Ativado]`, `[Sempre]`, `[Uma vez por turno]`, `[Centro]`, …) |
| Logs / prompts | `log_i18n.js` PT rules (`localizeLogMessagePt` / `localizePromptTextPt`) |
| Tutorial | `tutorial_pt.json` via `scripts/build_tutorial_pt.py` (from community BR export) |

Character names stay **English** (same as Spanish). Source sheet column: `text_br_edited` → merge via `python scripts/merge_text_pt.py`.

### French / fr (required — do not skip)

French (`fr`, `document.documentElement.lang = 'fr'`) is a **first-class locale**, same enforcement as Portuguese. **Every new or changed player-facing string must include French in the same change**.

| Surface | French files / fields |
|---------|----------------------|
| UI strings | `locales/fr.json` → `python scripts/inject_i18n_fr.py` → `STRINGS.fr` |
| Card rules text | `cards.json` → `text_fr` (brackets: `[À l'entrée]`, `[Début de Live]`, `[Activé]`, `[Permanent]`, `[Une fois par tour]`, `[Centre]`, …) |
| Logs / prompts | `log_i18n.js` FR rules (`localizeLogMessageFr` / `localizePromptTextFr`) |
| Tutorial | `tutorial_fr.json` |
| News | `news.json` posts → `title.fr` / `body.fr` |
| Stamps | `stamps_i18n.json` → `fr` |

Character names stay **English** (same as es/pt). See `docs/locales/FR_PROGRESS.md`.

### Where strings go

| Surface | English source | JA / ES / KO / ZH / TH / PT / FR |
|---------|----------------|-------------------------|
| Menus, screens, buttons, toasts, overlays | `i18n.js` → `STRINGS.en.*` | Matching `STRINGS.ja.*` / `STRINGS.es.*` / `STRINGS.ko.*` / `STRINGS.zh.*` / `STRINGS.th.*` / `STRINGS.pt.*` / `STRINGS.fr.*` |
| **Sticker Shop** (hub tile, shop screen, seal guide, deck convert-to-seal, related toasts/missions) | `STRINGS.en.hub.stickerShop*` + `STRINGS.en.sticker.*` (+ `toast.signInStickerShop` / `toast.sticker*`) | Same keys in **every** locale pack via `locales/{es,ko,zh,th,pt,fr}.json` → `inject_i18n_*.py`. Hub HTML uses `hub.sticker.title` / `hub.sticker.sub` (aliased from `hub.stickerShop` / `hub.stickerShopSub` in `mergeLocaleAliases`). |
| Static HTML labels | `data-i18n="dotted.key"` | Same key in `STRINGS.ja`, `STRINGS.es`, `STRINGS.ko`, `STRINGS.zh`, `STRINGS.th`, `STRINGS.pt`, and `STRINGS.fr` |
| JS-built UI | `t('dotted.key', { vars })` | Same |
| Interactive tutorial bubbles | `tutorial.json` dialogue | `tutorial_ja.json` / `tutorial_es.json` / `tutorial_ko.json` / `tutorial_zh.json` / `tutorial_th.json` / `tutorial_pt.json` / **`tutorial_fr.json`** |
| Legacy slideshow tutorial | `tutorial.*` | `tutorial.*` in all STRINGS packs **and/or** tutorial_*.json |
| Title-screen news posts | `news.json` | `en` / `ja` / `es` / `ko` / `zh` / `th` / `pt` / **`fr`** on each post |
| Server log lines | `log_i18n.js` | JA / ES / KO / ZH / TH / PT / **FR** rules + `STRINGS.*.log` |
| Card skill oracle text | `cards.json` `text` | `text_jp` / `text_es` / `text_ko` / `text_zh` / `text_th` / `text_pt` / **`text_fr`** with localized skill brackets matching `skillKw` |

### Checklist before finishing a feature with text

1. Add **`STRINGS.en` + `STRINGS.ja` + `STRINGS.es` + `STRINGS.ko` + `STRINGS.zh` + `STRINGS.th` + `STRINGS.pt` + `STRINGS.fr`** keys (or matching `tutorial_*.json` for interactive tutorial steps).
2. Wire HTML via **`data-i18n`** or JS via **`t()`** — avoid raw English in templates.
3. If UI is rebuilt on locale change, ensure **`refreshDynamicI18n()`** (or `onLocaleChange`) refreshes it.
4. Bump **`?v=`** on `i18n.js` / `tutorial_*.json` / `log_i18n.js` when those files change.
5. Run **`python scripts/extract_i18n_en.py`** then **`php scripts/validate_i18n.php`** after locale JSON changes (checks es, ko, zh, th, pt, **fr** against en). Sticker Shop belongs in this check (`sticker.*`, `hub.stickerShop*`, sticker toasts/missions) — do not leave those EN/JA-only.
6. For **interactive tutorial** steps:
   - Curate under **`locales/{locale}.json` → `tutorial.*`** (or `TUTORIAL_EXACT_OVERRIDES`).
   - Run **`python scripts/build_tutorial_locale_json.py --locale {locale}`**.
   - Run **`python scripts/validate_tutorial_i18n.py --locale {locale}`** (es/ko/zh/th/pt/**fr** leak checks).
   - Translate game terms/skill keywords; **do not** translate character names, group brands (Liella!, μ's), or Live/song titles in tutorial dialogue.
7. For **new/changed card rules text**: populate **`text_es` + `text_ko` + `text_zh` + `text_th` + `text_pt` + `text_fr`** in the same change (localized brackets; quoted names use locale name maps for ko/zh/th; pt/fr keep English names).

### Korean specifics

- `cardLocaleName` resolves KO via `KO_NAME_MAP` / `KO_SONG_MAP`.
- `cardLocaleText` → `card.text_ko`.
- Source of truth: `locales/ko.json` → `inject_i18n_ko.py`.

### Chinese specifics

- `cardLocaleName` resolves ZH via `ZH_NAME_MAP` / `ZH_SONG_MAP` (from `zh_names.json` / `zh_songs.json`).
- `cardLocaleType` → 成员 / Live / 能量.
- `cardLocaleText` → `card.text_zh`.
- Source of truth for UI: `locales/zh.json` → `inject_i18n_zh.py`.
- Skill bracket lock: 入场时 / 离场时 / Live开始 / Live成功 / 起动 / 永续 / 自动 / 每回合1次 / 中央 / Yell — keep identical across `text_zh`, `skillKw`, tutorial, and `log_i18n.js`.

### Thai specifics

- `cardLocaleName` resolves TH via `TH_NAME_MAP` / `TH_SONG_MAP` (from `th_names.json` / `th_songs.json`, once authored — see `docs/locales/TH_NAMES.md`).
- `cardLocaleText` → `card.text_th`.
- Source of truth for UI: `locales/th.json` → `inject_i18n_th.py`.
- Skill bracket lock (from the localization plan): เมื่อเข้าสนาม (On Enter) / เมื่อออกจากสนาม (On Leave) / เริ่ม Live (Live Start) / Live สำเร็จ (Live Success) / เปิดใช้ (Activated) / ต่อเนื่อง (Always) / เทิร์นละ 1 ครั้ง (Once per Turn) / เซ็นเตอร์ (Center) — keep identical across `text_th`, `skillKw`, tutorial, and `log_i18n.js` once each surface ships Thai. See `docs/locales/TH_PROGRESS.md` for the full glossary (game terms: เฟสหลัก, เฟส Live, เวที, ห้องรอ, พลังงาน, หัวใจ, เบลด, มัลลิแกน, สมาชิก, บาตองทัช, การแสดง, สำเร็จ).

### Do not

- Ship new menus, replay UI, error popups, or tutorial lines in English only.
- Add `data-i18n` without Japanese, Spanish, Korean, Chinese, Thai, Portuguese, **and French** strings.
- Rely on English fallback for JA/ES/KO/ZH/TH/PT/**FR** tutorial step ids (interactive tutorial stays EN for a locale until its `tutorial_*.json` ships).
- Ship new printed abilities without `text_es` / `text_ko` / `text_zh` / `text_th` / `text_pt` / **`text_fr`**.

### Title-screen news posts (`news.json`)

- Explain **what changes for the player** — gameplay, deck building, ranked/casual rules, balance.
- Use **card names and point values**, not file paths, repo names, deploy steps, or dev jargon.
- Do **not** mention `news.json`, Hostinger, git, APIs, or implementation details.
- Ship **en + ja + es + ko + zh + th + pt + fr** for every post title and body in the same change.
- **Card IDs** in post body are auto-linked — use exact catalog `card_no` values.
